These two both print the right thing for the Pass/Fail rule. What does the second one check first?

VERSION A:
if score >= 60:
    print("Pass")
else:
    print("Fail")

VERSION B:
if score < 60:
    print("Fail")
else:
    print("Pass")

For score = 70, what does VERSION B show?

if score < 60:
    print("Fail")
else:
    print("Pass")

For score = 40, what does VERSION B show?

if score < 60:
    print("Fail")
else:
    print("Pass")

Rewrite this to check the opposite first (temp below 30), keeping the meaning. Fill the comparison:

if temp ____ 30:
    print("Not hot")
else:
    print("Hot")
